ng but now  it's all about to be made very very  clear and that's thanks to some big  changes that DC has r already made  starting with the biggest change or I  should say biggest two changes and that  is of course the iconic James Gunn and  Peter saffron are now co-partners that  officially have the helm in leading the  projects when it comes to DC Studios  they're in charge so needless to say  Walter Hamada is no longer in that  position and with the company but James  Gunn and Peter saffron have already done  so much for in 2dc with the short amount  of time that they've held this position  now something that I do need to address  first is that yesterday we did get some  pretty shocking news the news came last  night that Warner Brothers was scrapping  Wonder Woman 3 and Man of Steel 2.  however recent reports have come out  stating that James Gunn simply didn't  like the vision that they had for Wonder  Woman in Wonder Woman 3 and he didn't  think it was going to be that good  apparently he was supposed to be handed  an entire script for Wonder Woman 3 but  was only handed a few pieces of paper  that didn't really do any justice to the  character so he kind of decided to scrap  it but he does have plans for Wonder  Woman and the future of the DCU I'm  assuming it's a similar thing for Henry  Cavill Superman considering the fact  that he just got back to the DCU and it  was a pretty big deal to get him back  I'm assuming they're not just going to  get rid of him altogether I'm assuming  what was happening is that Man of Steel  2 simply wasn't coming together the way  that the DCU was going to be rebooted  and it didn't simply work with their  plans that does not mean Henry Cavill  Superman is gone they are simply doing  what is best to fit these characters and  proper stories in the DCU so this is  actually a good thing because these  decisions are coming from James Gunn and  Peter Safran so I know a lot of people  were panicking about these decisions but  I think they are good decisions James  Gunn has definitely been talked about a  lot in the news recently especially with  him being the producer of the Guardians  of the Galaxy Trilogy and the director  as well and most recently the awesome  Christmas special with the guardians but  of course him also giving us the suicide  squad for DC and The Peacemaker series  both of which were really awesome  however some fans are upset why he is  still a huge face for Marvel however he  has a great response to those remarks if  you know anything about James Gunn you  know that he is active on Twitter and he  calls people out a lot and he responds a  lot he basically wants to always have  the record set straight here was his  response to people telling him that he's  still at Marvel when he's now in charge  of DC he said in a tweet as was made  clear in all press until May I am both  DC and Marvel I've dedicated the  majority of the past 10 years of my life  to the Guardians Trilogy and I'm not  abandoning them or the thousands of  people who worked on them at the 11th  Hour the world won't end if you love  both and he's entirely right and like  I've mentioned he's already done a lot  for DC so James Gunn will still be a  part of Marvel until May but since he is  such a legend with what he's done with  the Guardians of the Galaxy he will  always be a part of Marvel at heart and  let's not downplay Peter South friend  because he has produced Big projects as  well like Shazam and The Suicide Squad  the second one that is and even more in  the horror side like Annabelle and  here's what's really cool these two  James and Peter will continue to help DC  produce DC content rather than just  overseeing everything they're going to  be Hands-On involved we also have to  give some credit to Dwayne Johnson AKA  Black Adam or the rock for helping DC  out at a pretty big time he brought us  Black Adam an action-packed film and  showed us that DCU film projects will  now be released in phases much like  Marvel does which is a great thing but  what's really awesome of course is that  he brought back Henry Cavill so you can  see big changes being made at DC but how  exactly is it going to be so different  than it was before well for one it is  now in the hands of true fans and the  people who are surrounding them like the  Rock and Henry Cavill who really want to  see this universe Excel people who have  proven track records of making great  superhero films and shows basically we  have EX experience and passion now  something that I feel DC kind of lacked  before in regards to the people and the  executives behind making the movie  decisions that is and another huge thing  is that everything is going to be a lot  more clear for the universe and how it's  connected in fact right now James Gunn  and Peter Safran are working on what  they call a Bible for DC they are almost  finished with it as well and this is  basically something that's going to help  guide us through every part of DC and  show how it's either all connected or  not this includes the films TV shows  animated series and games which is  another big announcement by James Gunn  that is going to very much impact the DC  Universe in a great way James Gunn  tweeted that everything that DC is going  to put out now is going to be tied to  the DCU that means the films and TV  shows an animated series will all tie  into the DC Universe basically like how  Marvel does it with the MCU and how they  are fluent across the board with their  continuity now James Gunn and Peter  saffron will will make things very  easier and more exciting to follow  throughout all the Realms of DC he even  says that some video games are going to  be tied to the DCU as well which is  really awesome however he did respond to  another tweet about the video games  being connected to the DCU and his  remark is that not all will be tied to  it so some video games and this makes  sense because sometimes it's okay to do  one-offs or other things to Branch out  but you could only Branch out so far  that is if you are going to have a truly  connected Universe a perfect example of  branching out is Robert Pattinson's the  Batman which is not connected to the DCU  it's a one-off project nonetheless it  was an amazing movie but the bottom line  is we are going to have more continuity  and more connections on the DC Universe  and to take this even further it does  look like they are going to kind of  clean up some things that they've  already done before because they're not  going to completely erase everything  that has happened before some stuff will  still connect however we are going to be  starting in Phase One black Adam  technically was the first project of  DC's phase one but they are still going  to connect some things of the past but  they're gonna have to clean it up a bit  and David zasloff has said that there's  not going to be four Batmans so they're  cleaning it up a bit just to make it  less confusing which is great but also  sad because I would have loved to have  seen four Batmans on screen at the same  time but I think it's the right choice  one final thing that is worth noting is  that channy Dungey talked about closing  a deal with Amazon to get animated  series for DC on Amazon Prime video that  would be another win for DC so they  definitely seem to have everything in  place to make the DCU fantastic and most  importantly they have the right people  in charge now who have passion and  experience in making good superhero  movies even great superhero movies so  the future is bright for DC hopefully  they can make a pretty big comeback and  it looks like they are and I'm  definitely here for it I'm ready for it  I love DC I love Marvel you can love  both it's okay and I'm ready for both of  them to be amazing but hey let me know  your thoughts about this in the comments  down below what do you think about DC  are they going to make a comeback or not  don't forget to like the video an